# Snyk authentication

## Dependency automation (weekly cron)

**No Snyk settings page. No Cursor secrets.**

- Automation runs `./scripts/run-dependency-scan.sh` (npm audit).
- Snyk scans the fix PR via the **Snyk GitHub App** integration automatically.

## GitHub Actions CI (optional)

Refresh OAuth from CLI when CI Snyk fails — no API token from settings:

```powershell
snyk auth
.\scripts\refresh-snyk-oauth-secret.ps1
```

OAuth expires ~1h; re-run when needed. For weekly cron, refreshing before the Monday CI run is enough.

## Long-lived API token (optional only)

If you prefer `SNYK_TOKEN` from [app.snyk.io/account](https://app.snyk.io/account): `./scripts/set-snyk-github-secret.sh`. Not required for automation.

## On any Snyk request

1. Default path: npm audit in automation + Snyk GitHub App on PRs.
2. CI auth: `snyk auth` + refresh script (not settings page).
3. Setup guide: `docs/security/snyk-automation-setup.md`.
